Z||000000||Bruce||02-11-2001||03:18 PM||||Armed with a promise of "24-7" service and a Sunday morning appointment, I drove 1 1/2 hrs to West Coast Fieros. After circling the block twice, knocking on every possible door, and calling the business number, I finally gave up. What kind of slap-dick operation has so little integrity and consideration, and not even a business sign to indicate the location? <BR>Maybe the numerous unanswered phone calls, e-mails, and $140 Flowmaster muffler should have been a tip-off. Perhaps they have  the luxury of turning away $1000 of business, but based on the location and general shoddy appearance of their "business," I doubt it.<BR>Maybe George can open a Southern Calif. Fiero Shop!||||reg||1
Z||000001||gabriel||02-11-2001||04:06 PM||||This is exactly my concern in my earlier post.  Look under this post: chris west?<P>&lt;B&gt;I've read excellent reviews on thier products & support, but have seen concerns re. speed. Not horsepower -speed of response.&lt;/B&gt;<P>If you had an actual appointment & they blew it off, then this only adds to my concerns.<P>And I'm on the East coast!<BR>Thanks for the post.<P>I'm just not wired to wait, wait, wait & then wait some more. Patience is not one of my few virtues.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Other have written that West Coast is very busy, and I can understand that completely.  I had a business as well, & I can understand how that goes, but these little things are red flags to me.  I'll call tomorrow & see what they have to say about est. time of delivery.||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||02-11-2001||10:13 PM||||Yep, the shop is dificult to find. No doubt about it. We circle around for quite some time before we happenedupon it, and we only realy found it by going up to the shop that had a couple of dissasembled Fieros outside. Too bad he can't even kick a couple of bucks for spraypaint and some stencils to put the name on the door. He does do good work, though.||||reg||1
