Z||000008||c m west||02-12-2001||04:50 PM||||well guys what can I say, you have every right to put us down- after all were here for you, and if it wasnt for you guys we wouldnt be here at all - now to answer several of the remarks - <P>Bruce - my appologies for not greeting you here personaly on a Sunday. West Coast Fiero was at the SEMA show in Long Beach. Pat, our resident-transient ( giving a homeless lawyer a chance to turn his life around ) was here ALL day to welcome you - and I dont know how you could miss the fieros out front.<P>now, about the fieros out front:<P>Black 87 GT;<BR> customer works for a Petersen publication, went out and bought a Fiero to have us throw in every one of our pruducts into to be displayed and photographed in an upcoming Pontiac Special at the time - well - 8 months later he ran out of money when he bought a house, so instead of saying " hey, come pick up this half-built ****  box " we decided to work with him, were simply storing at as he pays it of - were not complete ass-holes here.<P>red 86 SE:<BR> presently having 3800 Series 1 motor being built on the side, owned by steve, one of the employees here<P>Black 86 SE<BR> 19 year old customer who has more time to use hid dads truck to get were he needs to go than to come by and pick it up after we rebuilt the transmission a second time<P>forklift out side:<BR> last I remembered - THIS WAS A MACHINE SHOP<P> As far as painting a logo on the door, this we would do if we OWNED the building and did not share it with Prime Marine. on any WEEKDAY you will see a 3' x 8' banner proudly dissplaying WEST COAST FIERO as well as out phone number, email address, website, and address, that is clearly marked atop the building as well (13456) <P>  so Bruce, I am sorry that I was not here on a Sunday for you, and because I am sorry I will be here everyday from now on 7 days a week, 18 hours a day, like I have been doing.You just happened to catch me while I gave myself a day of for the first time in 4 months, as far as Pat not answering the phones or the door on a Sunday, I will have words with him<P> as for everyone else, please bear with us as we are still integrating with Fiero Motorsports||||reg||4
Z||000009||dman||02-12-2001||05:55 PM||||Hello everyone. As a forum member, I'd just like to go on record as saying that everyone at West Coast Fieros has been a pleasure to speak with. Since I am in SoCal I actually find it much more convenient to simply call or drop by and visit their shop. Chris seems to be a very busy person but has -always- had time to answer my questions whenever I called or dropped by.<P>The ease I found in communicating with Chris was based on the simple fact that I was able to talk -directly- with him; either face to face or on the telephone. While they may have a website and an email address, I've found that the easiest way to get a question answered was to simply call. Just because it may be easy and convenient to write an email doesn't mean that the person you are writing the email to will reply. Not everyone is as connected to the internet as the Forum members seem to be. It is nice to hear that someone at West Coast Fieros is coming here to say that they are working on it (you guys really need to).<P>While the store front may not be all flash and glitter, the work performed at West Coast is 1st class. These guys aren't some greasy "slap-dick" operation. The expertise and know-how these guys possess is great. I'm glad the the Fiero community has such an asset as Chris West and West Coast Fieros here in Southern California.<P>I'm sorry Bruce that you had a bad experience. I'm not disputing or arguing with you, in fact I think it was a pretty bad mixup. I'm simply going on record to provide a counterpoint; to simply provide a differing opinion, a positive opinion about West Coast Fieros. Your message title read, "My advice about West Coast Fiero". Well my advice to fellow forum members is call the shop, speak with them. THEN make up your mind about whether you want to take your business to them.<P>I hope this doesn't cause a flame, its not my intent to do so.<P>Happy Fieros everybody.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Bruce||02-12-2001||06:42 PM||||I knocked, walked, waited, and called; all to no avail. If you make an appointment and a promise, stick with it or give me some satisfaction that the promised work will be done.<BR>All I know is that you promised to be there all day Sunday. Offering me an excuse on Monday is fairly weak if you made a committment on Saturday. Four hours wasted on a Sunday sits pretty uncomfortably with me.||||reg||1
Z||000011||c m west||02-12-2001||10:14 PM||||well bruce what can I say, any repair shop that I can think of is either closed or open for a few hours on Sundays, I do appologize for not being here - remeber  - walk a mile in someone elses shoes, that way when he gets pissed you will be a mile away and he will be barefoot =-)<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero<BR>( the guy keeping the wheels greased around here )||||reg||1
